---
// Walks one transaction's two signatures, step by step. Every size here is a
// parameter from FIPS 204 (ML-DSA-65) or FIPS 205 (SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s), and
// the repo constants in crates/crypto-pq/src/suite/ match them. No signature
// bytes are shown: the gateway has no transaction method, and no testnet
// transaction was captured for this page.
//
// Nothing here verifies a signature. Verification runs in the node.
import StarlightPage from "@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro";

// ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204, Table 2): k = 6 rows, l = 5 columns, 256 coefficients per polynomial.
const mlPk = { rho: 32, t1: 6 * 256 * 10 / 8 }; // t1 coefficients are 10 bits
const mlSig = { ctilde: 48, z: 5 * 256 * 20 / 8, hints: 61 }; // z coefficients are 20 bits; hints = omega + k
const mlTotal = mlSig.ctilde + mlSig.z + mlSig.hints;

// SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s (FIPS 205, Table 1 and 2): n = 16, h = 63 in d = 7 layers of h' = 9,
// FORS with k = 14 trees of height a = 12, Winternitz w = 16, len = 35 chains.
const n = 16;
const fors = 14 * (12 + 1) * n; // 14 trees: a secret leaf and a 12-node path each
const layer = (9 + 35) * n; // per layer: 9 authentication nodes and one WOTS+ signature (35 chains)
const slhSig = { r: n, fors, layers: 7, layer, total: n + fors + 7 * layer };
const slhPk = 2 * n;
---

<StarlightPage frontmatter={{ title: "Post-quantum signatures, step by step", description: "One Maya2C transaction carries an ML-DSA-65 and an SLH-DSA signature. This page walks through each check, with the real parameter sizes from FIPS 204 and FIPS 205.", template: "splash" }}>
  {/* not-content: Starlight's prose rhythm (a top margin on every sibling)
      misaligned the step chips and padded the cards; this page lays itself out.
      The page title is Starlight's h1; "Two locks" is the lede, not a second heading. */}
  <section class="sg not-content" aria-label="Signature walkthrough">
    <header class="sg-head">
      <p class="sg-kicker">Two locks on every transaction</p>
      <p class="sg-sub">A transaction is written only if both signatures check out. Four steps, with the real sizes.</p>
    </header>

    <nav class="sg-steps" aria-label="Steps">
      <button type="button" data-step="0" aria-current="step">1 · Message</button>
      <button type="button" data-step="1">2 · ML-DSA-65</button>
      <button type="button" data-step="2">3 · SLH-DSA</button>
      <button type="button" data-step="3">4 · Both checks</button>
    </nav>

    <article class="sg-panel" data-panel="0">
      <h2>The message</h2>
      <p>The signatures cover the transaction's signing bytes. Both algorithms sign the same message. Nothing is signed twice over different data.</p>
      <p class="sg-note">The SLH-DSA signer uses the deterministic variant with an empty FIPS 205 context (<code>crates/crypto-pq/src/sig.rs</code>, around line 203).</p>
    </article>

    <article class="sg-panel" data-panel="1" hidden>
      <h2>ML-DSA-65 · lattice</h2>
      <p>A lattice signature is a vector of polynomials. Each polynomial has 256 coefficients.</p>
      <div class="bars" role="img" aria-label={`Public key ${mlPk.rho + mlPk.t1} bytes, signature ${mlTotal} bytes`}>
        <p class="bar-label">Public key · {mlPk.rho + mlPk.t1} bytes</p>
        <div class="bar"><span style={`flex:${mlPk.rho}`} class="seg a">ρ {mlPk.rho}</span><span style={`flex:${mlPk.t1}`} class="seg b">t₁ · 6 polynomials, 10 bits each · {mlPk.t1}</span></div>
        <p class="bar-label">Signature · {mlTotal} bytes</p>
        <div class="bar"><span style={`flex:${mlSig.ctilde}`} class="seg a">c̃ {mlSig.ctilde}</span><span style={`flex:${mlSig.z}`} class="seg b">z · 5 polynomials, 20 bits each · {mlSig.z}</span><span style={`flex:${mlSig.hints}`} class="seg c">h {mlSig.hints}</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sg-note">FIPS 204, Table 2: ML-DSA-65 public key 1,952 bytes, signature 3,309 bytes. The repo constant is <code>ML_DSA_65_SIGNATURE_LEN</code> (3309).</p>
    </article>

    <article class="sg-panel" data-panel="2" hidden>
      <h2>SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s · hash tree</h2>
      <p>No lattice here: the signature is built from hashes alone. A few-time signature (FORS) is wrapped by a hypertree of seven layers. Each layer is a tree of height 9, so the whole tree has height 63.</p>
      <div class="tree" role="img" aria-label="Seven hypertree layers of height 9, above 14 FORS trees of 4096 leaves each">
        <div class="fors"><span>FORS · 14 trees · 2<sup>12</sup> leaves each</span></div>
        {Array.from({ length: 7 }, (_, i) => <div class="layer"><span>layer {i + 1} · height 9</span></div>)}
      </div>
      <div class="bar" aria-hidden="true">
        <span style={`flex:${slhSig.r}`} class="seg a">R {slhSig.r}</span>
        <span style={`flex:${slhSig.fors}`} class="seg b">FORS {slhSig.fors}</span>
        <span style={`flex:${slhSig.layers * slhSig.layer}`} class="seg c">7 layers × {slhSig.layer}</span>
      </div>
      <p class="sg-note">Signature {slhSig.total} bytes = R {slhSig.r} + FORS {slhSig.fors} + 7 × {slhSig.layer}. Public key {slhPk} bytes. FIPS 205, Table 2 gives 7,856 bytes; <code>SHA2_128S_SIGNATURE_LEN</code> is 7856 in the repo.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="sg-panel" data-panel="3" hidden>
      <h2>Both checks must pass</h2>
      <p>A transaction is accepted only when the ML-DSA-65 check and the SLH-DSA check both pass. If either fails, the transaction is not written.</p>
      <ul class="sg-checks">
        <li><strong>ML-DSA-65</strong> verifies against its public key, in the node.</li>
        <li><strong>SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s</strong> verifies against its public key, in the node.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="sg-note"><strong>Not done on this page:</strong> no client-side verification. Nothing in this page checks a signature, and no cryptography runs in the browser. The implementations are tested against NIST known-answer vectors in <code>crates/crypto-pq/tests/acvp_tests.rs</code>.</p>
    </article>

    {/* No lookup form until the public gateway has a method for it: a field the
        page itself says cannot work reads as broken (design critique, L02). */}
    <p class="sg-note">Looking up a transaction by hash is not available yet: the public gateway has no method for it (<a href="/guides/api/">API reference</a>).</p>

    <p class="sg-foot"><a href="/guides/signatures/">The guide to signatures</a> · <a href="/reference/hybrid-signatures/">Hybrid signatures</a> · <a href="/health/">Live health</a></p>
  </section>

  <script>
    const buttons = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".sg-steps button"));
    const panels = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".sg-panel"));
    function show(i: number) {
      panels.forEach((p, k) => { p.hidden = k !== i; });
      buttons.forEach((b, k) => { if (k === i) b.setAttribute("aria-current", "step"); else b.removeAttribute("aria-current"); });
    }
    buttons.forEach((b) => b.addEventListener("click", () => show(Number(b.dataset.step))));
  </script>

  <style>
    .sg { max-width: 920px; margin: 0 auto; display: grid; gap: 28px; padding: 8px 0 64px; color: var(--text); }
    .sg-kicker { font: 500 12px/1 var(--mono); letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--gold); margin: 0; }
    .sg-sub { font: 400 var(--type-body-lg-size)/1.55 var(--sans); color: var(--text-2); margin: 8px 0 0; max-width: 60ch; }
    .sg-note { font: 400 14px/1.55 var(--sans); color: var(--muted); margin: 8px 0 0; }
    .sg-note a { color: var(--accent-text); }
    .sg code { font: 500 12.5px var(--mono); color: var(--accent-text); }
    /* One height for every chip; the current one is marked by fill and ring only. */
    .sg-steps { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; }
    .sg-steps button { box-sizing: border-box; height: 44px; margin: 0; font: 600 13px var(--sans); padding: 0 14px; border-radius: var(--r-pill); border: 1px solid var(--border-control, var(--text-3)); background: var(--surface-1); color: var(--text-2); cursor: pointer; transition: border-color var(--dur-1) var(--ease), color var(--dur-1) var(--ease); }
    .sg-steps button:hover { color: var(--text); }
    .sg-steps button[aria-current="step"] { color: var(--text); border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--accent); background: var(--accent-subtle); }
    .sg-panel { padding: clamp(20px, 3vw, 30px); border-radius: var(--r-lg); border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface-1); box-shadow: var(--shadow-md); }
    .sg-panel h2 { font: 650 22px/1.2 var(--display); margin: 0 0 12px; color: var(--text); }
    .sg-panel > :first-child { margin-top: 0; }
    .sg-panel p { font: 400 15px/1.6 var(--sans); color: var(--lede); margin: 8px 0; }
    .bars { display: grid; gap: 8px; margin: 18px 0; }
    .bar-label { font: 500 12px var(--mono); color: var(--muted); margin: 6px 0 0 !important; }
    .bar { display: flex; width: 100%; min-height: 40px; border-radius: var(--r-s); overflow: hidden; border: 1px solid var(--glass-edge); }
    /* Each segment pairs a fill with a label colour measured on it in both
       themes: text on the pale teal, on-accent on teal, the page bg on bronze. */
    .seg { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 0 6px; font: 500 11.5px/1.2 var(--mono); text-align: center; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap; }
    .seg.a { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 22%, var(--surface-1)); color: var(--text); }
    .seg.b { background: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); }
    .seg.c { background: var(--bronze); color: var(--bg); }
    .tree { display: grid; gap: 6px; margin: 18px 0; max-width: 520px; }
    .tree > div { padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: var(--r-md); border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface-1); font: 500 12.5px var(--mono); color: var(--text); }
    .tree .fors { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bronze) 16%, var(--surface-1)); }
    .tree .layer { margin-left: 24px; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 12%, var(--surface-1)); }
    .sg-checks { margin: 12px 0; padding-left: 20px; font: 400 15px/1.7 var(--sans); color: var(--lede); }
    .sg-foot { font: 500 13px var(--sans); color: var(--muted); }
    .sg-foot a { color: var(--cherenkov-hi); }
  </style>
</StarlightPage>
